        "start_column": 11,
        "end_column": 99
      },
      "finding": "subprocess.run([\"git\", \"status\", \"--short\"], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)",
      "explanation": "The use of `subprocess.run` without proper input validation can be risky. An attacker could potentially provide malicious input to the `git status` command, leading to unexpected behavior or security issues, such as executing unwanted commands or causing the system to run in an unintended state.",
      "remediation": "To mitigate this, ensure that the input to the `git status` command is validated or sanitized. Alternatively, use safer alternatives like `subprocess.Popen` with carefully crafted command execution, or consider using higher-level libraries that abstract away direct command execution, such as `gitpython`.",
      "code_snippet": "\n\ndef status():\n    return subprocess.run([\"git\", \"status\", \"--short\"], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":",
      "intent": null,
